  "evidence": [
    "Pinned632DB0-632F97: routed peer flags are BYTE, system type is DWORD632E56 with102/103 branches632F18/632F1F. Existing packet[0] switch incorrectly makes both unreachable. SDK dplay.h DPMSG_* definitions supply original field identities and offset witnesses.",
    "Peer table has header count lowbyte+8 and40-byte records at+C: ID+0,name+4,flagDWORD+24. Count is freshly read after each insertion; creation message dpId is freshly read after GetPlayerName. Preserve these reloads, callback order, failed-provider return ignored and zero/null text handling. No new safety checks or capacity clamp.",
    "GetPlayerName632EDB receives9BE4EC and advertised100-byte capacity then response long name is read+0C632EF1. Replace fixed image pointer with source-owned aligned DPNAME plus byte response storage;100 is observed API capacity, not asserted full original allocation extent. Source object start binding added only from observed emitted symbol; no fabricated exact data claim.",
    "Keep all existing functions, API signatures, original spans/claims/bindings and unrelated bytes unchanged. Whole Net owner measurement baseline/current, fresh full build/link, targeted actual-body host controls with high-word, reload and failed-provider damage cases, independent review and source/object continuity are required. Temporary local matching regressions from justified structural recovery retain historical obligations; no demotion or claimed full-game acceptance."
  ],
  "intent": "Recover complete system/peer message dispatch using original widths, typed protocol records and genuine player-name response storage, preserving original unsafe/error paths.",
